/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Never commit client binaries or extracted game assets.
/client-patched/
/research/fixtures/*.bin
/research/fixtures/*.wz
/out/
*.pdb

# Ghidra projects are large binaries/databases
/research/ghidra/

# probe run artifacts
probe.log
probe.err

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Socket capture from -Sockets runs
sockets.log

# pktmon captures are large binaries; the decoded text summary goes in fixtures instead
/research/pktmon/

# The live database. Accounts (argon2id hashes) and characters - real state, not source,
# and it holds password hashes, so it never goes in the repo.
maplecw.db
maplecw.db-wal
maplecw.db-shm

# Client exit forensics, rewritten by every run. Was tracked by accident until
# 2026-08-19, so it showed as pending after every launch. Runs worth keeping are
# copied into research/fixtures/ under a name that says what they prove.
client-exit.log

# Login server run log
login.log
login.log.err
# Sign-in service run log. Added with the service itself on 2026-08-29;
# it was the one server log nothing ignored.
auth.log
auth.log.err
world.log
# One log per channel: channel 0 keeps world.log, the rest are world-ch<N>.log.
world-ch*.log
world-ch*.log.err
world.log.err

# Name tables extracted from String.wz by tools/dump_names.py. Game data, not project
# source - the repo carries the code to regenerate them, not the content.
gm-handbook/

# A side target directory, used to build the servers when a run still holds
# target/release open. See tools/channel_smoke.py MAPLECW_BIN_DIR.
/target-smoke

# tools/package-server.ps1's build tree. Separate from target/ on purpose: RUSTFLAGS is part
# of cargo's fingerprint, so sharing one would make every static/dynamic switch a full
# rebuild - and would leave target/release holding statically linked binaries that the dev
# scripts then run without anyone noticing the difference.
/target-static

# The launcher now archives the previous run here instead of deleting it. Generated
# per-run output, not source - runs worth keeping are copied into research/fixtures/.
previous-runs/

# Crash dumps from WER LocalDumps. Full dumps under page heap are ~1 GB each.
/dumps/

# The hook logs unconditionally, so `cargo test -p grap-stub` leaves one of these in
# the crate directory. The real one lives in client-patched/ and is gitignored with it.
maplecw-hook.log

# The packaged client, built by tools/make-installer.ps1. 551 MB, and it is a
# BUILD OUTPUT - the repo carries the code, not the content, same arrangement as
# gm-handbook/. Regenerate it rather than committing it.
MapleClient.zip

# Agent working directories. CLAUDE.md has a whole section on why a scratchpad is
# dangerous - a script run from one imports ITS copy of a repo tool, silently, and a
# stale copy answers instead of raising. It must never be committed, and a common
# filename in there is a collision between concurrent agents, not just clutter.
scratchpad/

# Stray minidumps in the SOURCE tree. `minidump.rs`'s self-test writes to a fixed
# scratch directory and flakes under concurrent `cargo test`; a killed run leaves a
# dump beside the crate. They are up to 1.3 GB and none of them belongs in git.
crates/**/*.dmp
